#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"The reference to the Bridge is a **setter method** `+setModbus+`; therefore "
"`+@GenerateTargetsFromReferences+` contains the reference name `+"
"\"Modbus\"+`."
msgstr ""
"Die Referenz auf die Bridge ist eine **Setter-Methode** `+setModbus+`; daher "
"steht in `+@GenerateTargetsFromReferences+` der Referenzname `+\"Modbus\"+`."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"`+super.activate(…, config.modbusUnitId())+` registers the device with the "
"Bridge. The base class creates the protocol once on first access via "
"`+defineModbusProtocol()+` and then keeps it. Values from the Config that "
"influence the protocol (here `+invert+`) must therefore be set **before** "
"`+super.activate+`."
msgstr ""
"`+super.activate(…, config.modbusUnitId())+` meldet das Gerät bei der Bridge "
"an. Das Protokoll erzeugt die Basisklasse einmalig beim ersten Zugriff über "
"`+defineModbusProtocol()+` und behält es danach. Werte aus der Config, die "
"das Protokoll beeinflussen (hier `+invert+`), müssen deshalb **vor** "
"`+super.activate+` gesetzt sein."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"`+ElectricityMeter.calculateAverageVoltageFromPhases(this)+` is an example "
"of calculated Channels: if the device only provides phase values, totals or "
"averages are created via callback."
msgstr ""
"`+ElectricityMeter.calculateAverageVoltageFromPhases(this)+` ist ein "
"Beispiel für berechnete Channels: Liefert das Gerät nur Phasenwerte, "
"entstehen Summen- oder Mittelwerte per Callback."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tasks"
msgstr "Tasks"

#. type: #sec-tasks
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid "A task is a Modbus request over a contiguous register range."
msgstr ""
"Ein Task ist eine Modbus-Anfrage über einen zusammenhängenden "
"Registerbereich."

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Class\n"
"| Function code\n"
"| Purpose\n"
"\n"
"| `+FC3ReadRegistersTask+`\n"
"| 3\n"
"| read holding registers (most common case)\n"
"| `+FC4ReadInputRegistersTask+`\n"
"| 4\n"
"| read input registers\n"
"| `+FC1ReadCoilsTask+`, `+FC2ReadInputsTask+`\n"
"| 1, 2\n"
"| read coils or digital inputs\n"
"| `+FC6WriteRegisterTask+`\n"
"| 6\n"
"| write one register\n"
"| `+FC16WriteRegistersTask+`\n"
"| 16\n"
"| write several registers\n"
"| `+FC5WriteCoilTask+`\n"
"| 5\n"
"| write one coil\n"
msgstr ""
"| Klasse\n"
"| Funktionscode\n"
"| Zweck\n"
"\n"
"| `+FC3ReadRegistersTask+`\n"
"| 3\n"
"| Holding-Register lesen (häufigster Fall)\n"
"| `+FC4ReadInputRegistersTask+`\n"
"| 4\n"
"| Input-Register lesen\n"
"| `+FC1ReadCoilsTask+`, `+FC2ReadInputsTask+`\n"
"| 1, 2\n"
"| Coils bzw. digitale Eingänge lesen\n"
"| `+FC6WriteRegisterTask+`\n"
"| 6\n"
"| ein Register schreiben\n"
"| `+FC16WriteRegistersTask+`\n"
"| 16\n"
"| mehrere Register schreiben\n"
"| `+FC5WriteCoilTask+`\n"
"| 5\n"
"| eine Coil schreiben\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"The elements of a task must follow each other **without gaps**. Registers "
"that are not needed are filled with `+new DummyRegisterElement(from, to)+`. "
"A read request over a larger range is usually faster than many small ones; "
"some devices, however, limit the number of registers per request or reject "
"ranges with undefined registers."
msgstr ""
"Die Elemente eines Tasks müssen **lückenlos** aufeinander folgen. Nicht "
"benötigte Register füllt man mit `+new DummyRegisterElement(von, bis)+` auf. "
"Ein Leseauftrag über einen größeren Bereich ist meist schneller als viele "
"kleine; manche Geräte begrenzen aber die Anzahl Register je Anfrage oder "
"lehnen Bereiche mit undefinierten Registern ab."

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Priority and scheduling"
msgstr "Priorität und Zeitplanung"

#. type: #sec-priority-and-scheduling
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"The Bridge schedules the tasks per Cycle (`+ModbusWorker+`, "
"`+TasksSupplierImpl+`):"
msgstr ""
"Die Bridge plant die Tasks pro Zyklus (`+ModbusWorker+`, "
"`+TasksSupplierImpl+`):"

#. type: #sec-priority-and-scheduling
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"**Write tasks** run as early as possible, directly after "
"`+TOPIC_CYCLE_EXECUTE_WRITE+`."
msgstr ""
"**Schreib-Tasks** laufen so früh wie möglich, direkt nach "
"`+TOPIC_CYCLE_EXECUTE_WRITE+`."

#. type: #sec-priority-and-scheduling
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"**Read tasks** run as late as possible so that the values are fresh for "
"`+TOPIC_CYCLE_BEFORE_PROCESS_IMAGE+`."
msgstr ""
"**Lese-Tasks** laufen so spät wie möglich, damit die Werte zu "
"`+TOPIC_CYCLE_BEFORE_PROCESS_IMAGE+` frisch sind."

#. type: #sec-priority-and-scheduling
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid "`+Priority.HIGH+`: the read task runs in **every** Cycle."
msgstr "`+Priority.HIGH+`: Lese-Task läuft in **jedem** Zyklus."

#. type: #sec-priority-and-scheduling
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"`+Priority.LOW+`: per Cycle, **one** LOW task of the whole Bridge runs, in "
"turn. With many LOW tasks, it therefore takes correspondingly many Cycles "
"until a value is renewed. Suitable for meter readings, serial numbers, limit "
"values."
msgstr ""
"`+Priority.LOW+`: pro Zyklus läuft **ein** LOW-Task der ganzen Bridge, "
"reihum. Bei vielen LOW-Tasks dauert es also entsprechend viele Zyklen, bis "
"ein Wert erneuert ist. Geeignet für Zählerstände, Seriennummern, Grenzwerte."

#. type: #sec-priority-and-scheduling
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"If the cycle time is not sufficient for all tasks, the Bridge sets the "
"Channel `+CycleTimeIsTooShort+`; `+CycleDelay+` shows the delay."
msgstr ""
"Reicht die Zykluszeit nicht für alle Tasks, setzt die Bridge den Channel "
"`+CycleTimeIsTooShort+`; `+CycleDelay+` zeigt die Verzögerung."

#. type: #sec-priority-and-scheduling
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"A device that repeatedly does not respond is considered defective. Only a "
"single random task is then attempted occasionally so that it does not block "
"the bus for the other devices."
msgstr ""
"Ein Gerät, das wiederholt nicht antwortet, gilt als defekt. Von ihm wird "
"dann nur ab und zu ein einzelner zufälliger Task versucht, damit es den Bus "
"für die anderen Geräte nicht blockiert."

#. type: #sec-priority-and-scheduling
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"After how many read errors the values become invalid (`+null+`) is set on "
"the Bridge (“Invalidate elements after how many read Errors?”)."
msgstr ""
"Nach wie vielen Lesefehlern die Werte ungültig (`+null+`) werden, stellt man "
"an der Bridge ein („Invalidate elements after how many read Errors?“)."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
